From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Cache queue objects by default

Use cached firmware mappings for queue metadata, matching the captured
macOS queue class. Keep compute, TA, FS and work-ring cache bits off.

The J604 queue-only experiment passed changing-output compute and pixel
checks, three timing rounds, two reproduction runs and the full suite
with zero faults. Full-suite render.light fell from 131.8 to 87.3 us and
compute.light from 56.9 to 40.7 us; heavy rows stayed within one percent.
The separate compute-object cache bit remains off after its lifetime
failure. Override aurora.g16_fw_cached=0 to restore uncached queues.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
index dbc5e1fbc3..0eb5e094ee 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
@@ -288,8 +288,8 @@ fn init(module: &'static kernel::ThisModule) -> impl PinInit<Self, Error> {
             description: "G16: bounded cached compute arena retention until reboot (diagnostic)",
         },
         g16_fw_cached: u32 {
-            default: 0,
-            description: "G16: cached kinds: 1 queue 2 compute 4 TA 8 FS 16 ring (default 0)",
+            default: 1,
+            description: "G16: cached kinds: 1 queue 2 compute 4 TA 8 FS 16 ring (default 1)",
         },
         g16_init_dump: u32 {
             default: 0,
-- 
